WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:05.770
Strong power is eventually overthrown
by even stronger power.

00:05.770 --> 00:09.300
I've seen more than enough of that.

00:09.300 --> 00:13.600
Doctor, is making a thing like that really right?

00:14.340 --> 00:15.970
Now!

00:23.180 --> 00:26.420
Please, give me your help.

00:26.420 --> 00:29.550
Come with me to Ulvarx.

00:42.640 --> 00:50.250
Far away from the town where I was born

00:50.250 --> 00:53.420
I am singing

00:53.420 --> 01:01.060
Tucking my weak heart and my wavering feelings

01:01.060 --> 01:04.330
Away in my pocket

01:04.330 --> 01:09.860
Toward where I hear someone calling me

01:09.860 --> 01:14.900
Toward the unknown road

01:14.900 --> 01:20.340
I'll walk

01:20.340 --> 01:25.750
I'll move forward

01:25.750 --> 01:30.590
Not for someone else's sake

01:30.590 --> 01:36.060
But just as I am, so that I can take pride

01:36.060 --> 01:41.530
Just as the sun rises at dawn

01:41.530 --> 01:46.770
I pick out a melody with my voice

01:46.770 --> 01:50.800
Ephemerally yet strongly

01:52.440 --> 01:55.970
I live

02:01.680 --> 02:05.520
Episode 41
The Thought That Possessed Him

02:07.690 --> 02:09.320
Dukeham...

02:10.930 --> 02:14.880
To think you'd bring us the wielder of Amir Gaul...

02:15.630 --> 02:17.930
I'm grateful, Ginga.

02:19.000 --> 02:22.600
Ginga, we have to obey Tusk here.

02:22.600 --> 02:25.010
What?! What are you talking about?!

02:25.010 --> 02:26.570
That's not funny!

02:26.570 --> 02:28.200
Rambos!

02:33.720 --> 02:37.010
Stop it! You'll break my system!

02:37.950 --> 02:40.390
Doctor, just what do you think you're doing?!

02:40.390 --> 02:44.590
They rated my technology very highly!

02:44.590 --> 02:46.660
If I can put this technology to full use,

02:46.660 --> 02:49.900
I don't care if it's Tusk backing me!

02:49.900 --> 02:52.070
Are you really okay with that?!

02:52.070 --> 02:54.200
What the hell have you been fighting for, then?!

02:54.200 --> 02:57.000
I have nothing but my research!

02:58.470 --> 03:00.100
Doctor!

03:04.210 --> 03:05.250
Panopria!

03:05.250 --> 03:06.870
Creeper!

03:13.890 --> 03:17.190
That's not Amir Gaul.

03:34.740 --> 03:36.370
Karen!

03:40.920 --> 03:42.220
Karen!

03:42.220 --> 03:44.010
Are you okay?!

03:44.620 --> 03:47.420
Yeah, who's Karen?

03:55.000 --> 03:57.170
Damn it, quit being so stubborn!

03:57.170 --> 03:59.130
Zed, over here!

03:59.130 --> 04:00.670
Let's withdraw for now!

04:00.670 --> 04:02.040
Right!

04:02.040 --> 04:03.660
Wait!

04:06.840 --> 04:07.940
After them!

04:07.940 --> 04:09.740
Don't let them escape!

04:22.790 --> 04:24.260
I'm sorry.

04:24.260 --> 04:25.990
I let the enemy get away.

04:25.990 --> 04:27.200
It's all right.

04:27.200 --> 04:28.660
You fought well.

04:28.660 --> 04:30.970
I do not deserve such praise, sir.

04:30.970 --> 04:36.270
But I won't let things end here, Zed.

04:40.310 --> 04:43.280
We won't be easily found here.

04:43.850 --> 04:46.510
Let's rest here for a while.

04:46.510 --> 04:49.150
Roya, is your shoulder okay?

04:49.150 --> 04:50.950
Yeah, I'm fine.

04:50.950 --> 04:52.790
It's just a scratch.

04:52.790 --> 04:55.090
Oh, good.

04:56.090 --> 04:59.260
Was that man Doctor Vendar?

04:59.260 --> 05:04.470
Yeah, but to think that he'd betray us...

05:04.470 --> 05:08.500
In the end, he was only thinking of his research.

05:08.500 --> 05:12.460
It was easy for him to switch over
to Dukeham's side.

05:14.180 --> 05:15.940
Dukeham...

05:15.940 --> 05:19.280
Do you know that guy?

05:19.280 --> 05:20.910
Yeah...

05:21.980 --> 05:25.280
I'm originally from Tusk.

05:25.990 --> 05:28.320
But then you and I are...

05:28.320 --> 05:29.990
Yeah...

05:29.990 --> 05:33.830
Dukeham was my superior officer
in my old military unit,

05:33.830 --> 05:38.790
and he's also the man who killed Karen,
the one I loved most in this world.

05:39.170 --> 05:40.970
What?

05:40.970 --> 05:45.240
Oh, that's right, earlier you looked
at me and said " Karen" ...

05:45.240 --> 05:50.380
Yep, Karen looked just like you, Roya.

05:50.380 --> 05:52.010
What?

05:56.320 --> 05:58.290
Split up and track them down.

05:58.290 --> 05:59.910
Yes, sir!

06:00.460 --> 06:02.360
Zed...

06:02.360 --> 06:05.330
The man who possesses Amir Gaul, eh?

06:06.160 --> 06:11.270
Dukeham was the most warmhearted
of Tusk's officials,

06:11.270 --> 06:15.240
and he cherished hardworking subordinates.

06:15.240 --> 06:18.540
I respected him for that.

06:19.440 --> 06:21.740
Until Karen was killed, that is.

06:23.440 --> 06:27.740
She was a member of the Dukeham's unit too.

06:41.500 --> 06:44.950
As we fought together, we became
attracted to each other.

06:45.900 --> 06:48.030
Eventually, we fell in love.

06:50.170 --> 06:52.610
One day Karen went to Neotopia

06:52.610 --> 06:55.580
under orders to destroy their defensive system.

06:59.710 --> 07:04.520
But she failed in her mission,
and came back wounded.

07:06.350 --> 07:07.660
Karen!

07:07.660 --> 07:09.290
I am sorry.

07:09.290 --> 07:11.960
I have failed in my mission.

07:11.960 --> 07:14.000
The protections on Neotopia's defensive system

07:14.000 --> 07:16.100
are stronger than we'd anticipated,

07:16.100 --> 07:19.730
and I'm afraid destroying it may be
almost impossible.

07:22.640 --> 07:25.810
You just said " impossible, " didn't you?

07:25.810 --> 07:27.680
No, sir, I...

07:27.680 --> 07:32.310
I don't need anyone who'd close off her own
future with the word " impossible" !

07:38.420 --> 07:40.760
Please, wait, Lord Dukeham!

07:40.760 --> 07:43.360
I will take over Karen's mission.

07:43.360 --> 07:44.960
I'll accomplish it without fail!

07:44.960 --> 07:48.090
So please, forgive Karen.

07:53.470 --> 07:56.740
As usual, you have a nice look in your eyes,

07:56.740 --> 07:59.210
that passionate look I like.

08:02.340 --> 08:04.980
Dukeham was a warmhearted man,

08:04.980 --> 08:10.220
but the moment someone says they're
giving up, he shows no mercy.

08:10.220 --> 08:13.850
I was desperate to protect Karen.

08:16.420 --> 08:19.720
But I failed too.

08:28.700 --> 08:33.000
I lost consciousness after a Neotopian attack.

08:34.480 --> 08:37.770
And when I came to...

08:47.190 --> 08:48.820
Karen!

08:49.890 --> 08:53.760
Dukeham executed her right in front of my eyes.

08:53.760 --> 08:58.220
That was our punishment for failing our mission.

09:02.800 --> 09:04.430
Ginga, don't !

09:12.350 --> 09:14.450
I turned my back on Tusk.

09:14.450 --> 09:18.220
Eventually, I ended up here in Ulvarx.

09:18.220 --> 09:22.490
I changed my tattered body
for a mechanized one,

09:22.490 --> 09:24.960
swearing vengeance on Dukeham.

09:30.530 --> 09:34.100
Who is that Ginga boy?

09:34.100 --> 09:39.640
Ginga was once the best man in my unit.

09:39.640 --> 09:41.410
Oh, really?

09:41.410 --> 09:44.150
He's a traitor now.

09:44.150 --> 09:46.510
To show my love for my subordinate,

09:46.510 --> 09:49.380
I'll at least kill him with my own hands.

09:49.380 --> 09:51.550
An overly complicated way to put it.

09:51.550 --> 09:54.520
Don't you just mean,
"He's a traitor so I'll kill him" ?

09:54.520 --> 09:57.650
I don't particularly care whether
you understand me or not.

09:58.360 --> 10:00.330
Oh, I see.

10:00.860 --> 10:07.340
I didn't think you Tuskans would appreciate
my technology so much.

10:07.340 --> 10:09.300
I'm very happy.

10:11.110 --> 10:16.740
With this system, ruling over all the
territories is within your reach.

10:17.380 --> 10:20.350
I see you're quite confident.

10:20.350 --> 10:25.290
However, I hear a composite spirit
went off the rails in Neotopia.

10:25.290 --> 10:27.720
That Ex Machina was incomplete!

10:27.720 --> 10:31.030
The rampage happened because an
inexperienced Ulvarxan took it...

10:31.030 --> 10:34.400
This system had better be all right.

10:34.400 --> 10:37.570
If another rampage were to occur...

10:37.570 --> 10:39.200
I trust you understand the consequences.

10:39.200 --> 10:41.300
O..Of course!

10:41.300 --> 10:43.200
I have absolute confidence in it.

10:43.200 --> 10:46.170
Then, will you show me some proof?

10:46.610 --> 10:49.040
Proof?

10:49.040 --> 10:53.250
If it can fully control the strongest
of the key spirits,

10:53.250 --> 10:57.050
it will prove just how completely you've
perfected the system, correct?

10:57.920 --> 10:59.890
What do you think?

11:01.090 --> 11:02.890
Very well.

11:04.860 --> 11:06.660
I look forward to it.

11:18.710 --> 11:20.610
Lady Sagiri!

11:20.610 --> 11:23.410
It appears you are awake.

11:25.680 --> 11:29.140
You slept for quite some time.

11:29.920 --> 11:32.050
Where am I?

11:32.050 --> 11:34.390
Who are you, Gramps?

11:34.390 --> 11:36.560
We are the Seekers,

11:36.560 --> 11:41.830
the descendants of those who left your
homeland Rion to travel the skies.

11:41.830 --> 11:43.800
Seekers?

11:47.200 --> 11:50.870
What I am about to tell you is very important.

11:50.870 --> 11:53.210
Please listen carefully.

11:53.210 --> 11:58.780
You are of the Seekers' royal bloodline,
and you were born in Rion.

11:58.780 --> 12:01.480
Zymot's invasions were progressing,

12:01.480 --> 12:05.790
and the consuls feared for your safety.

12:05.790 --> 12:09.690
They placed you in Galva's care,
and you were raised in secret.

12:09.690 --> 12:11.320
Galva...

12:13.890 --> 12:17.770
Hey, where are Galva and the others?!

12:17.770 --> 12:20.730
You are the only one who survived.

12:21.840 --> 12:27.510
And you made your way through this
war-torn world to return here.

12:27.510 --> 12:32.510
You are the one who will become
the savior of the Seekers.

12:32.510 --> 12:35.180
Me, the savior?

12:35.180 --> 12:37.650
Yes, that's right.

12:38.520 --> 12:41.360
I don't really get it.

12:41.360 --> 12:43.660
Never mind, where's Noah?

12:43.660 --> 12:44.790
Noah?

12:44.790 --> 12:48.300
Yeah! Where's Noah?

12:48.300 --> 12:49.920
Sara?

12:52.600 --> 12:54.540
This woman...

12:54.540 --> 12:58.070
Sara, where is the man called " Noah" ?

12:58.070 --> 13:00.240
He is dead.

13:00.240 --> 13:01.780
That's a lie!

13:01.780 --> 13:04.180
I won't believe what you say!

13:04.180 --> 13:06.150
Noah is alive!

13:06.150 --> 13:08.270
I know he's alive!

13:12.220 --> 13:15.020
So, now what?

13:15.020 --> 13:17.760
You saw in Neotopia what fearsome monsters

13:17.760 --> 13:23.100
that system of the Doctor's creates.

13:23.100 --> 13:24.500
Yeah...

13:24.500 --> 13:27.430
Now that he's gone over to Tusk,

13:27.430 --> 13:30.100
the only thing we can do is...

13:30.100 --> 13:33.570
So, our only choice is to bust that thing then?

13:33.570 --> 13:35.110
Yeah...

13:35.110 --> 13:40.150
The only thing that kind of power
can do is breed tragedy.

13:40.150 --> 13:43.450
It's claimed too many of my comrades.

13:45.920 --> 13:48.060
I'll distract Dukeham.

13:48.060 --> 13:52.860
While I'm doing that, you two go to the
central lab and destroy the system.

13:52.860 --> 13:54.660
Got it!

13:55.400 --> 13:57.000
Now, Sara.

13:57.000 --> 14:02.340
Our goal is to ensure that the key spirits
are never gathered in one place.

14:02.340 --> 14:06.070
But Tusk is planning to take
possession of all of them,

14:06.070 --> 14:09.870
and get their unknown power.

14:10.210 --> 14:13.410
There are six key spirits in this world.

14:13.410 --> 14:16.210
They must never all come together!

14:16.880 --> 14:19.680
When that happens, everything will perish.

14:20.790 --> 14:25.930
Sara, will you put a stop to Tusk's scheme for us?

14:25.930 --> 14:27.720
As you wish.

14:32.430 --> 14:33.770
Lord Dukeham...

14:33.770 --> 14:35.070
What is it?

14:35.070 --> 14:37.470
Ginga has shown himself.

14:37.470 --> 14:38.810
He's on the periphery.

14:38.810 --> 14:39.970
What?

14:39.970 --> 14:43.240
Yes, and, well...

14:43.240 --> 14:44.550
Well, what?!

14:44.550 --> 14:48.000
He says he'd like to fight you one-on-one, sir.

14:50.850 --> 14:54.020
Interesting, that's my Ginga.

14:54.020 --> 14:57.060
Instruct the troops to leave him be until I get there.

14:57.060 --> 14:58.680
Yes, sir!

15:09.400 --> 15:12.370
Hey, what's your plan to destroy it?

15:17.950 --> 15:18.950
What's that?!

15:18.950 --> 15:20.010
A spirit!

15:20.010 --> 15:22.310
Go get them, Amir Gaul!

15:23.020 --> 15:26.320
So, the "plan" is just to use Amir Gaul, huh?

15:30.390 --> 15:32.960
Asking me for a one-on-one fight...

15:32.960 --> 15:35.230
That's just like you, Ginga.

15:35.230 --> 15:39.030
I'll send you to the next life with my own hands.

15:39.870 --> 15:41.340
Don't make me laugh!

15:41.340 --> 15:45.970
I'll bring you down with the new power
that I've gained here!

15:46.870 --> 15:48.500
Goliath!

15:51.150 --> 15:52.940
I see...

15:53.750 --> 15:55.370
Doom Blitz!

15:57.580 --> 15:59.550
Here I come, Dukeham!

16:07.390 --> 16:10.060
Ah, Amir Gaul!

16:10.060 --> 16:12.570
That's Great Tusker's ...

16:12.570 --> 16:16.340
I'd like to see you hurry up and control him
with that system you're so proud of.

16:16.340 --> 16:18.310
Already on it.

16:26.450 --> 16:30.080
That's the technique Helic and
the others were using.

16:30.650 --> 16:31.790
That's right,

16:31.790 --> 16:35.410
but this latest model does more
than just hold them captive.

16:42.760 --> 16:44.260
What are you trying to do?

16:44.260 --> 16:45.270
Damn it!

16:45.270 --> 16:46.600
Zed!

16:46.600 --> 16:48.070
Amir Gaul!

16:48.070 --> 16:49.170
Stop it!

16:49.170 --> 16:51.410
You sit back and watch too!

16:51.410 --> 16:55.740
Watch a key spirit being fully controlled.

16:55.740 --> 16:56.840
Why, you...

16:56.840 --> 16:59.140
You'd better be a good boy, Zed.

16:59.980 --> 17:02.950
If you want her head to stay on her body, that is.

17:05.120 --> 17:06.920
That's low!

17:26.870 --> 17:28.500
Goliath!

17:38.650 --> 17:42.780
In the end, this is all your petty hatred amounts to.

17:43.590 --> 17:46.790
Die here, you traitorous scum.

17:46.790 --> 17:48.900
Shut up!

17:48.900 --> 17:52.100
First you pretended to be merciful,

17:52.100 --> 17:54.700
and then in the end you killed her!

17:54.700 --> 17:57.200
You're an underhanded bastard!

17:57.200 --> 17:59.110
What are you talking about?

17:59.110 --> 18:01.810
I didn't kill Karen.

18:01.810 --> 18:03.010
You liar!

18:03.010 --> 18:04.810
It's not a lie!

18:05.080 --> 18:07.950
Lord Dukeham was not the one who killed Karen.

18:07.950 --> 18:09.750
Who the hell was it, then?!

18:10.250 --> 18:12.520
You killed her!

18:12.520 --> 18:14.150
What?

18:19.130 --> 18:20.930
Now, Vendar...

18:20.930 --> 18:24.000
Hurry up and make Amir Gaul
do something for us.

18:24.000 --> 18:25.630
Don't rush me.

18:25.630 --> 18:29.260
First off, how about you open your eyes?

18:29.840 --> 18:34.800
And after I've made you do my bidding,
I'll make you part of Ex Machina!

18:38.080 --> 18:40.050
Amir Gaul is...

18:40.980 --> 18:43.020
What are you saying, Miguel?

18:43.020 --> 18:44.890
What do you mean by that?!

18:44.890 --> 18:49.620
After you went to Neotopia in Karen's place,

18:49.620 --> 18:52.420
she appealed to Lord Dukeham.

18:53.490 --> 18:55.960
She said she wanted to try her mission again,

18:55.960 --> 18:59.130
that she wanted him to let her
do it together with you,

18:59.130 --> 19:03.090
but Lord Dukeham did not grant her
permission to go with you.

19:03.600 --> 19:06.770
Yet, she went after you anyway.

19:06.770 --> 19:08.900
She disobeyed orders to do it.

19:10.210 --> 19:12.610
Since Lord Dukeham cares more than most
for his subordinates,

19:12.610 --> 19:14.780
he was worried for the two of you.

19:14.780 --> 19:17.750
He and I went to Neotopia together.

19:20.850 --> 19:23.480
But we were too late.

19:27.790 --> 19:30.730
She was probably trying to protect you.

19:30.730 --> 19:33.360
Karen was killed by the enemy.

19:33.800 --> 19:34.940
That's a lie.

19:34.940 --> 19:36.730
No, it's not.

19:37.070 --> 19:42.480
Then, Karen to shield me...

19:42.480 --> 19:44.600
trying to protect me...

19:47.550 --> 19:50.020
He's as good as dead.

19:57.190 --> 20:00.230
Stop, you'll harm my lab!

20:00.230 --> 20:02.200
So, it was impossible after all.

20:02.200 --> 20:04.990
That's the strongest of the key spirits for you.

20:09.500 --> 20:11.130
Amir Gaul!

20:17.610 --> 20:20.780
Ultimately, you're nothing but a scientist
that Neotopia gave up on.

20:20.780 --> 20:23.080
I was wrong to expect anything of you.

20:24.120 --> 20:27.290
No, my system was perfect!

20:27.290 --> 20:29.080
It just...

20:32.430 --> 20:33.530
Zed!

20:33.530 --> 20:35.560
Are you okay, Roya?

20:35.560 --> 20:37.360
Yeah, I'm fine.

20:38.100 --> 20:40.070
What's going on?

20:42.700 --> 20:44.500
That's Amir Gaul!

20:45.110 --> 20:46.730
Doom Blitz!

20:53.480 --> 20:55.280
Amir Gaul!

21:05.790 --> 21:09.420
He took out my Doom Blitz with just one hit?!

21:10.160 --> 21:13.100
Let's withdraw for now, Lord Dukeham.

21:13.100 --> 21:16.000
No, the fight is not over yet!

21:16.000 --> 21:17.800
But, sir...

21:19.670 --> 21:22.380
This building will collapse before long.

21:22.380 --> 21:24.110
Let's evacuate, quickly!

21:24.110 --> 21:26.740
Damn you, Zed!

21:27.910 --> 21:31.150
Where did Ginga go?!

21:31.150 --> 21:32.620
We have to get out of here fast.

21:32.620 --> 21:34.190
This place is toast!

21:34.190 --> 21:37.690
We have to look for Ginga!

21:37.690 --> 21:39.320
Amir Gaul!

21:57.340 --> 22:00.310
I killed her.

22:01.320 --> 22:04.770
I killed Karen.

22:16.860 --> 22:18.970
Amir Gaul, go back!

22:18.970 --> 22:21.300
Ginga is still back there!

22:21.300 --> 22:23.100
Amir Gaul!

22:23.840 --> 22:26.140
Amir Gaul!

22:39.620 --> 22:42.020
I just wanted to get away

22:42.020 --> 22:44.920
From that troublesome place

22:45.860 --> 22:49.230
And flap my wings

22:49.230 --> 22:54.430
How many times have I scolded myself

22:54.430 --> 23:00.070
For still being so immature?

23:01.140 --> 23:05.980
I'll just move with all I've got

23:05.980 --> 23:11.620
Towards that promised place

23:11.620 --> 23:17.220
Ours are true wings

23:17.220 --> 23:24.000
Of very, very beautiful feathers

23:24.000 --> 23:26.700
So we won't succumb

23:26.700 --> 23:33.740
To even the greatest, most intense gust of wind

23:33.740 --> 23:43.820
We must fly far, far away with all we've got

23:43.820 --> 23:49.560
See, now we're one with the wind

23:49.560 --> 23:54.630
And we can look back and laugh at those days

23:54.630 --> 23:57.930
We choked back so many tears

23:59.930 --> 24:03.890
All the way to the ends of the world

24:18.020 --> 24:20.950
Next Time
A Small Savior

24:18.020 --> 24:20.950


Next time, "A Small Savior"
